We use hands for all the interactions we perform. How could we design interactions for the foot and use them together with hands?

FAND (Foot Associated Neural Device) is a haptic interface device that allows users to operate a computer using all four limbs. The device predicts learned motion gestures to perform interactions with drawing or VR apps.
